e when you decide to do the  surgery you own the complications as  well  you hopefully understood  that the risks were understood and  necessary  given the reason you did the surgery but  you don't just walk away and say that's  somebody else's problem  let's watch a little more uh and mehdi  hassan actually makes this point to john  bolton  you say it's simply not right but the  reality is hundreds of thousands of  iraqis died there was torture  millions of refugees and that did follow  from the decision by george w bush dick  cheney and others in the administration  like yourself to invade iraq  hundreds of thousands of people died and  just to go back to my question which you  didn't answer  do those deaths never do those deaths  never weigh on your conscience was my  question which you didn't answer  no i did answer and i'll answer it again  since you didn't seem to listen to it  the the fact was after the overthrow of  saddam hussein  a number of decisions could have been  made in different ways i don't believe  in u.s participation in nation  i think nations have to build themselves  now this is just outrageous bolton  doesn't believe in us nation building  during the iraq war which bolton by the  way says was four weeks long  during the iraq war all these neocons  were talking about  spreading democracy to iraq uh and he  now says he doesn't believe in nation  building and he wasn't the guy involved  in those decisions  he knew what the bush administration  planned  to do and for him to now say well they  didn't  involve me in those decisions give me a  break  he believes in four weeks of military  and saying we're done  and now it's up to them and he has  nothing to do with it and it continues  in this  bizarre way and had the united states  followed through with that approach  rather than  engaging in extensive nation building  the outcome  i think could well have been very  different but delay  what happened in iraq on the single  decision to overthrow sad